A||N||16||AusFiero||Sorry I haven't answered most enquiries today - We are battling to save our house||||9||
Z||000000||AusFiero||08-08-2001||08:08 AM||||    I have had a lot of Fiero parts enquiries today that I have not been able to answer. With good reason. We have 100 KMH (60 MPH) winds happening and have been battling to stop things blowing away plus I was back in hospital for a while, but am ok again now. <BR>    I am currently waiting for the State Emergency Service to get here as our tin roof is starting to flap in the wind and is getting noisier by the hour. It is not looking good at present for our house as I am not in any fit state to be up on a roof battling such high winds. I just hope they get here soon enough.<BR>    Thre is nothing more I can do now but sit and wait. Is 10pm and there is huge problems everywhre because of the wind and the SES can only be so many places at once.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||9
Z||000001||Songman||08-08-2001||09:21 AM||||Good luck, Jim... Seems like it is always something, don't it?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jaygee79||08-08-2001||09:30 AM||||Good luck.  We'll be praying for you and your family.||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||08-08-2001||09:33 AM||||Yeah I can't seem to win a trick these days Songman. At least the SES is here now. They are throwing ropes over the roof and sandbagged it down. So it ain't going anywhere for now at least. <BR>Hospital was a sh!t though. I broke my own golden rule of do not do too  much manual labour in a day until I am fully recovered. Well between working on the body kit this morning and an intended rest this aftertoon, well the afternoon rest didn't happen when this wind picked up and I sorta made myself rather ill. Was alright after a rest in hospital but have been told until I am fully recovered I must go to the hospital if ever in doubt. Just precautionary measures.||||reg||1
Z||000004||8Ball||08-08-2001||09:55 AM||||Aus,<P>I know that everyone here on the forum appreaciates the work your doing, But for our sakes, <BR>Your sake, And your Famalies Sake, SLOW down man. Nobody is going to think less of you if it takes a while for the parts to come out.<BR>I am sure I speak for all of us when I say that your ALOT more important to us than some Fiero parts. I know you want to get them out, and I know you need and want to make some money. But man your health is WAY to important. Please take it easy, and good luck with the wind. I had the misfortune of being in the middle of a tornado about 6 or 7 years ago in which the house I was in lost it's entire roof. The tornado litteraly took it off in one piece and set it down 3 houses over in one piece. It was NOT FUN!!<P>Randy||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||08-08-2001||01:21 PM||||Just sit down, kick back and relax! Have a beer or two (or something stiffer!)<BR>No real rush on anything, right?<P>Be well first!<P>OH, I cleaned my yard after I took those pics! Put everything back in the barn! (among other places)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||08-08-2001||02:34 PM||||Jim,<P>You're not listening to us. <BR>Please take care of yourself. <BR>Your health is far too important to risk by trying to overdo things. <BR>We're here.<BR>We'll wait. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||grinthock||08-08-2001||03:11 PM||||DAMMIT!!! AUS will you cut it out!! Honestly dude, how many times do we all need to tell you to TAKE IT EASY, take some time to rest, those of us who have ordered, UNDERSTAND!!! And the last thing we need is something to happen to you...<BR>I also speak for all of us in saying that if we were able to, you would have everyone last one of us there helping to save your house.<P>Prayers and stuff come from EVERYONE on PFF to you, and your family, but damnit how many times does your wife, your doctor AND US have to tell you to SIT YOUR ASS DOWN AND REST!!!<P><BR>Have a nice day.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||08-08-2001||03:12 PM||||That's right, Jim! After you get my scoops and rocker out, take a break! heheh<P>Just teasing! I only wish I had ordered them!<P>Don't make us come over there! We will you know!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroMaster88||08-08-2001||04:33 PM||||Yeah Aus....dont make youself sick over us.  YOu need to relax man!  We all want you to recover...not make yourself worse.  I hope your luck gets better man.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||9
Z||000010||AusFiero||08-08-2001||06:59 PM||||Whew. <BR>    Well our house survived the night and the winds have died down. Didn't get a lot of sleep with bits of the roof making so much noise. Plus I had to go outside at 4AM and tie my garden shed down before it became some of the refuse in the street.<BR>    Time to go out and assess the damage soon, then yes I am doing as you's  are advising and taking a day off. Kids are at their grandmothers house and this afternoon a big nap is in order with peace and quiet. <BR>    I know there must be some sort of damage around the place because our pool has all sorts of things floating around in it. Neighbours across the road, well their BBQ lid is now on the road and seems every male in the street (Is a small Culde Sac street) is not going to work today. Must be a fair bit of damage around.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||14
Z||000011||Sage||08-08-2001||07:29 PM||||Take 2 or even 3 days off.  All of life is based on...rest and activity.  When you walk, one leg rests, while the other acts.  When you breathe, the outbreath is the rest, the in, the activity.  You can only stay awake so long, then whether you want to or not, you WILL go to sleep.  Rest and activity.  Get your rest, then act.<P>Take care and have a good one!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||08-08-2001||08:39 PM||||Aus- did you receive my order? If so, put it on the "back burner" and take some time for the family! <p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Doni Hagan||08-08-2001||09:32 PM||||Aus...<P>I e-mailed you before logging on to the Forum. That explains why I hadn't heard from you. Take your time, man. Everyone understands priorities. Good luck and God bless. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||FieroGTguy||08-09-2001||02:00 AM||||If you need to make money while you rest, you can do something like the Fiero Factory did awhile back... <P>Sell vouchers that are redeemable for a higher value of your future products.  Refundable after a given amount of time if the products aren't available, and if the person isn't interested on the available products you could supply?<P>Say, $75 vouchers worth $100 at time of purchase?  It should at least cover your tooling and effort that you have put into everything so far.<P>Just an idea,<BR>Greg||||reg||1
Z||000015||Butter||08-09-2001||10:50 AM||||AusFiero,<BR>My old man told me once when I was first leaving home some advise that has always helped me through life especially during those difficult times.  He said "Take care of number one."  So take care of yourself first.  I got things I would like your advise on and I want you to be there when the time comes.<P>Now about that roof of yours.  I got tired of nailing down the shop roof I have been using so I tried those screws with the metal and rubber washers on them.  It helped me with my shop roof maintenance problems.  Have someone else do it if needed just take care of yourself.  Wish you the best.||||reg||1
Z||000016||FieroHeather||08-09-2001||06:27 PM||||Get better Aus<P>Im thinkin of ya...<P>Rest easy my Australian friend  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
